CODE-8 | SINGLE-PAGE FOOD ORDERING WEB APP FRONTEND-ONLY DEVELOPMENT
PROMPT

ROLE Act as a senior frontend software engineer, product designer and
UI/UX specialist. Build a polished, responsive, single-page web
application for CODE-8, using the supplied one-page CODE-8 promotional
flyer as the primary source of truth for the brand, menu and business
details.

PROJECT GOAL Create one complete, attractive, mobile-first webpage that
introduces CODE-8, displays its food and drinks, explains pickup and
delivery, and makes it easy for customers to place an order through
WhatsApp or call the business.

SCOPE: FRONTEND ONLY This is strictly a frontend project. Do not build a
backend, database, server, authentication system, admin dashboard,
payment gateway or delivery-management system. Do not claim that an
order is stored or processed by CODE-8 automatically. All interactions
must work in the browser. The final deliverable is one single-page
application, not a multi-page website.

SOURCE CONTENT: USE THE FLYER EXACTLY Brand name: CODE-8 Main slogan:
Good Food, Great Vibes. Brand line: Our Code-Ate. Service message: Pick
Up & Delivery

Menu items shown on the flyer: - Jollof Rice - Amala - Yogurt - Zobo -
Yam Porridge - Ewa Agoyin - Pie - Donut - Popcorn - And Much More…

Brand promises: - Fresh Meals Daily - Affordable & Pocket Friendly
Meals - Quality Food Always

Call / WhatsApp: 08069489508 Business address: 8thGear Hub, 41 CMD Road,
Magodo Secretariat, Lagos.

Do not invent prices, opening hours, delivery charges, social media
handles, ingredients, dietary claims or other business details that are
not supplied. Do not omit or rename any of the listed menu items.
Display prices only if they are later supplied; otherwise use wording
such as “Contact us for price” or omit price labels.

DESIGN DIRECTION Use the flyer as the visual and brand reference.
Recreate its distinctive visual character in a cleaner, modern web
layout: - Deep forest green as the primary brand colour. - Bright golden
yellow as the main accent and call-to-action colour. - Warm
cream/off-white as the page background. - Dark charcoal or near-black
for readable text. - Bold, confident CODE-8 branding. - Appetising,
realistic food photography, especially Nigerian meals and snacks. -
Subtle leaf or food-inspired decorative details only where they improve
the design. - Rounded food cards, clear typography, generous spacing and
restrained shadows. - Smooth, subtle hover and scroll effects. - Strong
contrast and accessible text sizes.

Avoid a generic restaurant template, excessive gradients, clutter,
over-animation or an artificial-looking interface. The result should
feel like a professionally designed Nigerian food brand website and
remain faithful to the supplied flyer.

SINGLE-PAGE LAYOUT Build the page as one continuous experience with
smooth anchor navigation. Use the following sections in this order.

1.  STICKY HEADER

-   CODE-8 wordmark/logo treatment.
-   Navigation links that scroll to sections on the same page: Home,
    Menu, About, Pickup & Delivery, Contact.
-   A prominent yellow “Order Now” button.
-   On mobile, use a compact menu or simple responsive navigation.
-   Keep the header readable and usable on small screens.

If the original logo file is not available as a separate asset, create a
tasteful text-based CODE-8 wordmark inspired by the flyer. Do not claim
that a recreated wordmark is the original logo.

2.  HERO SECTION Create a visually striking first screen. Main headline:
    “Good Food, Great Vibes.” Supporting brand line: “Our Code-Ate.”
    Supporting copy: “Enjoy delicious meals, snacks and refreshing
    drinks from CODE-8. Available for pickup and delivery.” Show a
    high-quality food arrangement inspired by the flyer, featuring a
    selection of Nigerian meals, snacks and drinks. Add two clear calls
    to action:

-   “Explore Our Menu” should scroll to the menu section.
-   “Order on WhatsApp” should open WhatsApp using the official business
    number. Include a clear “Pickup & Delivery” visual label.

3.  MENU SECTION Heading: “Explore Our Menu” Supporting line: “Good
    food, great vibes. Find something delicious.” Display all flyer menu
