FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS - The page must be a real, working frontend, not
a static mockup. - All navigation links must scroll to the correct
section. - The header must remain usable on mobile. - Menu item
selection must work. - Quantity controls must work. - The order summary
must update immediately. - Removing items must work. - The WhatsApp
message must accurately reflect the selected items and quantities. - The
pickup/delivery choice must be included in the WhatsApp message. - If
delivery is selected, request the customer’s delivery address before
opening WhatsApp. - Validate required fields and show clear, friendly
inline feedback. - Telephone and WhatsApp links must use the correct
business number. - Buttons must have real actions. Do not leave dead or
decorative buttons. - Provide visible hover, focus, active, loading
where relevant, and validation states. - Ensure the order panel is easy
to close and reopen. - Do not request or collect payment details.

TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS Use a modern frontend framework supported by the
development environment, preferably React with TypeScript and Tailwind
CSS. Use reusable components and a consistent design system. Use
client-side state for the menu selection and order summary. No backend,
database, API, authentication or payment integration.

The app must: - Work on mobile, tablet and desktop. - Load quickly. -
Use responsive image sizing and sensible image optimisation. - Have
accessible labels, semantic HTML and keyboard-operable controls. -
Maintain readable colour contrast. - Avoid horizontal overflow. -
Include useful empty states and form validation. - Handle missing or
failed food images gracefully. - Have no broken links, dead buttons or
browser console errors.

FINAL ACCEPTANCE CHECKLIST Before declaring the work complete, verify
that: 1. The result is one single-page webpage application. 2. The
design visibly reflects the supplied CODE-8 flyer. 3. All brand wording
and business details are accurate. 4. Every menu item from the flyer is
present. 5. No prices or business details have been invented. 6. All
page navigation works. 7. Customers can select menu items and change
quantities. 8. The order summary reflects the selected items correctly.
9. Pickup and delivery selection works. 10. Delivery address is
requested when delivery is selected. 11. The WhatsApp link opens the
correct CODE-8 number with a correctly formatted draft message. 12. The
telephone link opens the correct number. 13. The page is responsive and
accessible. 14. There is no backend, database, admin dashboard or real
payment functionality. 15. The page does not claim that an order or
payment has been completed automatically.

FINAL DIRECTION Deliver a polished, professional, visually memorable
single-page CODE-8 food ordering webpage. It should translate the
supplied flyer into an effective digital customer experience, preserve
the company’s identity and make it effortless for visitors to browse the
menu and contact CODE-8 to place an order.

